{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>This is the thing that HaShem commanded.</b> In parashat Matot, Rashi explained that all the prophets prophesied with ״כֹה אָמַר ה׳״, but Moses was added to them in that he prophesied with ״זֶה הַדָּבָר אֲשֶׁר צִוָּה״, because Moses saw the thing with his own eye in a clarifying mirror. And the reason Rashi did not explain the same for what is said here, ״זֶה הַדָּבָר״, is that the Mishkan does not indicate his prophecy, because the Holy One, blessed be He, had shown him the Mishkan on the mountain, as it is written (Exodus 25:9) ״כְּכֹל אֲשֶׁר אֲנִי מַרְאֶה אוֹתְךָ אֵת תַּבְנִית הַמִּשְׁכָּן״ etc. Therefore he said, ״זֶה הַדָּבָר אֲשֶׁר צִוָּה ה׳״ — as one who points with his finger at a thing that he saw with his own eyes, and this expression does not indicate any special excellence that was not found in the other prophets, for Ezekiel too saw the entire pattern of the Temple."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:25:20.459854982Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}